x1": 0.453475935828877, "y1": 0.13801652892561983}, {"text": "uestion 5.", "x0": 0.16149732620320856, "y0": 0.16115702479338842, "x1": 0.24171122994652405, "y1": 0.17107438016528925}, {"text": "(i) A particle moves in the x-axis with acceleration at position x given by", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.18760330578512396, "x1": 0.7754010695187166, "y1": 0.20165289256198346}, {"text": "xr 2", "x0": 0.45133689839572194, "y0": 0.22231404958677686, "x1": 0.5411764705882353, "y1": 0.23884297520661157}, {"text": "where p is a positive constant. If at zero time the particle is released from rest at", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.27603305785123966, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.2900826446280992}, {"text": "the point a = a derive formulae for", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.29421487603305785, "x1": 0.4449197860962567, "y1": 0.3082644628099174}, {"text": "(a) its velocity v at position", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.32148760330578513, "x1": 0.3850267379679144, "y1": 0.33553719008264465}, {"text": "(b) its position \u00ab at time t.", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.3487603305785124, "x1": 0.37219251336898396, "y1": 0.3628099173553719}, {"text": "(ii) The rise and fall of the tide at a certain harbour may be taken as simple harmonic,", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.3760330578512397, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.39008264462809916}, {"text": "the interval between s ive high tides being 12.5 hours. The harbour entrance", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.3942148760330578, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.40826446280991735}, {"text": "has a depth of 15 metres at high tide and 7 metres at low tide. If low tide occurs", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.412396694214876, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.42644628099173554}, {"text": "at 11 am, on a certain day find the earliest time thereafter that a ship requiring a", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.4305785123966942, "x1": 0.8577540106951872, "y1": 0.4446280991735537}, {"text": "minimum depth of 13 metres of water can pass through the entrance.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.4487603305785124, "x1": 0.7379679144385026, "y1": 0.4628099173553719}, {"text": "Question 6.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.4859504132231405, "x1": 0.24171122994652405, "y1": 0.4991735537190083}, {"text": "(i) Explain, with proof and with the aid of a diagram, why", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.512396694214876, "x1": 0.6491978609625668, "y1": 0.5264462809917355}, {"text": "cos a sina", "x0": 0.44171122994652406, "y0": 0.5504132231404959, "x1": 0.560427807486631, "y1": 0.5603305785123966}, {"text": "sina \u2014cosa@", "x0": 0.44171122994652406, "y0": 0.5685950413223141, "x1": 0.5614973262032086, "y1": 0.5785123966942148}, {"text": "is called a reflection matrix.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6033057851239669, "x1": 0.38288770053475935, "y1": 0.6140495867768595}, {"text": "(ii) Prove that the product of two reflection matrices represents a rotation.", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.631404958677686, "x1": 0.7807486631016043, "y1": 0.6454545454545455}, {"text": "(iii) Given A = [i 7 compute the elements of the matrix A\u00ae\"*4 where nis \u00ab", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.656198347107438, "x1": 0.8406417112299466, "y1": 0.6925619834710743}, {"text": "integer.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6942148760330579, "x1": 0.20748663101604278, "y1": 0.7074380165289256}, {"text": "Question 7.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7305785123966942, "x1": 0.24171122994652405, "y1": 0.743801652892562}, {"text": "(i) For the matrix F find the eigenvalues and corresponding eigenvectors.", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.7545454545454545, "x1": 0.8213903743315508, "y1": 0.7909090909090909}, {"text": "(ii) Prove that, in the Cartesian plane, the equation", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.8024793388429752, "x1": 0.5893048128342246, "y1": 0.8165289256198347}, {"text": "5a? + Gry + 5y? \u2014 dy =", "x0": 0.3711229946524064, "y0": 0.8363636363636363, "x1": 0.6160427807486631, 