ext": "uestion 9.", "x0": 0.16149732620320856, "y0": 0.4066115702479339, "x1": 0.24171122994652405, "y1": 0.41735537190082644}, {"text": "(i) Prove that the series > is convergent for s > 1.", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.4396694214876033, "x1": 0.613903743315508, "y1": 0.45454545454545453}, {"text": "nt", "x0": 0.3572192513368984, "y0": 0.4570247933884298, "x1": 0.3839572192513369, "y1": 0.4636363636363636}, {"text": "(ii) Determine whether the series", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.4768595041322314, "x1": 0.42780748663101603, "y1": 0.4909090909090909}, {"text": "is convergent or divergent.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.5661157024793388, "x1": 0.3700534759358289, "y1": 0.5801652892561984}, {"text": "(iii) It follows from part (3) that the seri", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.5933884297520661, "x1": 0.4844919786096257, "y1": 0.6074380165289256}, {"text": "Loa", "x0": 0.42566844919786095, "y0": 0.6239669421487604, "x1": 0.47914438502673795, "y1": 0.6338842975206611}, {"text": "preter", "x0": 0.37433155080213903, "y0": 0.6355371900826446, "x1": 0.5240641711229946, "y1": 0.6553719008264463}, {"text": "is convergent and, in fact, it is known that its sum is 77/6. It is also given that the", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6694214876033058, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.6851239669421487}, {"text": "sum of the first thousand terms of this 1,644 (with four-figure accuracy).", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.6884297520661157, "x1": 0.8556149732620321, "y1": 0.7033057851239669}, {"text": "Hence we obtain an approximation to the value of x from the following calculations:", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7074380165289256, "x1": 0.8556149732620321, "y1": 0.7214876033057851}, {"text": "6(1.644) = 9.864", "x0": 0.4320855614973262, "y0": 0.7272727272727273, "x1": 0.5711229946524065, "y1": 0.7537190082644628}, {"text": "V9.864 = 3.141 (to four-figure ac", "x0": 0.44278074866310163, "y0": 0.7611570247933884, "x1": 0.7229946524064171, "y1": 0.7768595041322314}, {"text": "and therefore 7 = 3.141 approximately.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.7900826446280992, "x1": 0.47914438502673795, "y1": 0.8041322314049587}, {"text": "Without using any other knowledge of the value of x, inve", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8173553719008264, "x1": 0.6588235294117647, "y1": 0.8314049586776859}, {"text": "igate the accuracy of", "x0": 0.6759358288770053, "y0": 0.8173553719008264, "x1": 0.8588235294117647, "y1": 0.8314049586776859}, {"text": "this approximation so obtained for", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.8355371900826446, "x1": 0.44171122994652406, "y1": 0.8495867768595041}, {"text": "(3) If w is a complex number i \u2014 1 indicate on the Argand diagram the points", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.8983471074380165, "x1": 0.8096256684491978, "y1": 0.912396694214876}], [{"text": "(ii) On the Argand diagram, P represents the complex number z and R the number", "x0": 0.14759358288770053, "y0": 0.12396694214876033, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.13801652892561983}, {"text": "and a square PQRS is drawn in the plane with PR as a diagonal. If P lies on", "x0": 0.17219251336898395, "y0": 0.14214876033057852, "x1": 0.8566844919786096, "y1": 0.15619834710743802}, {"text": "circle |2| = 2 prove that Q will lie on an ellipse whose equation has the form", "x0": 0.18502673796791444, "y0": 0.15950413223140497, "x1": 0.8320855614973262, "y1": 0.1743801652892562}, {"text": "2 42", "x0": 0.46203208556149733, "y0": 0.1933884297520661, "x1": 0.5155080213903743, "y1": 0.20082644628099172}, {"text": "and specify numerical values for @ and b.", "x0": 0.146524064171123, "y0": 0.2462809917355372, "x1": 0.493048128342246, "y1": 0.2603305785123967}]]